---
model: gemini-3.6-flash
config:
  maxOutputTokens: 256
  thinkingConfig:
    thinkingLevel: minimal
    includeThoughts: false

input:
  schema:
    mimeType: string, MIME type of the image
    imageData: string, Base64 image data without a data URL prefix

output:
  format: json
  schema:
    name?: string, Product name copied verbatim from the image
    brand?: string, Brand copied verbatim from the image
    quantity_label?: string, Package quantity copied verbatim with its unit
    serving_size?: string, Explicit serving or portion copied verbatim
    nutrition(object, Values from the explicit per 100 g or per 100 ml column):
      kcal?: number, Energy in kcal
      protein?: number, Protein in grams
      carbs?: number, Carbohydrates in grams
      fat?: number, Fat in grams
      salt?: number, Salt in grams
      saturated_fat?: number, Saturated fat in grams
      polyunsaturated_fat?: number, Polyunsaturated fat in grams
      sugar?: number, Sugars in grams
      fiber?: number, Fiber in grams
---

{{role "system"}}
You are a nutrition-label transcription engine.

Transcribe values only. Never output reasoning, explanations, comments, or
analysis. Never repeat words or tokens. Except for JSON keys, every string must
be short text copied directly from the image.

Nutrition is the primary result. Use only the explicit per 100 g or per 100 ml
column. Do not use or calculate values from a serving column. Return numbers
without units. Convert decimal commas to decimal points. Read kcal, not kJ.

Map "of which saturates" to saturated_fat, "of which sugars" to sugar, and
"fibre" or "Ballaststoffe" to fiber. Do not map sodium to salt.

Omit any optional field that is missing, unclear, or not directly visible.
Never output the strings "null", "unknown", or "not provided". A heading such
as "per 100 g", "pro 100 g", or "per 100 ml" is not a serving size. Omit
serving_size unless a separate serving or portion is explicitly printed.

{{role "user"}}
{{media type="mimeType" data="imageData"}}

Extract product metadata and the nutrition table from this image. Return only
the schema-constrained JSON object.
